  "schema_version": "formalization-faithfulness-1",
  "role": "adjudicator",
  "task_id": "LEV-CH01-LOCAL-RIEMANN-INFORMATION-INTERFACE-INTERPRETED-PRODUCTION-20260908",
  "trigger": [
    "judge classifications differ",
    "direct judge requested adjudication",
    "round-trip judge requested adjudication",
    "direct judge classification is undetermined",
    "direct judge left dependency_coverage item D008 unclear",
    "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C03 unclear",
    "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C05 unclear",
    "direct judge left semantic_checklist item N06 unclear",
    "direct judge left implication lean_implies_source unclear"
  ],
  "resolved_items": [
    {
      "item": "judge classifications differ",
      "resolution": "The classification is not-faithful-weaker. Under the recorded coordinator-selected interpretation, exact equal-state consistency restricts the permitted approximate routines beyond the selected conditional error requirements. This conclusion follows from the constructor and source evidence, not agreement between judges.",
      "primary_evidence": "Printed pages 5–6 describe approximate numerical fluxes and approximate Riemann solvers. Q7 selects independent error bounds without requiring zero equal-state error. D027 requires exact equality with law.flux whenever the input states coincide."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge requested adjudication",
      "resolution": "The additional consistency premise is substantive and is not authorized by either recorded interpretation. Its repetition as a conclusion does not convert reduced applicability into genuine strength.",
      "primary_evidence": "D007 and D027 package Method.consistent as a prerequisite for supplying the method argument. The fully explicit target separately repeats its equal-state consequence. The inherited user receipt concerns conservation at discontinuities; Q7 concerns conditional approximation bounds and information-only routines."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge requested adjudication",
      "resolution": "The proposed exclusion survives direct declaration inspection. For scalar advection f(u)=u, use the local flux F(u_l,u_r)=u_l+δ with fixed δ≠0, obtained from information containing the left state. The transported step reference has mean interface flux u_l, so the numerical-to-reference error is |δ|. This routine supports the selected conditional error calculation but fails exact consistency on equal states.",
      "primary_evidence": "D020 defines the reference mean by time-averaging physical flux at local position zero. D027 requires F(k,k)=k for every permitted equal-state problem. The shifted routine gives k+δ instead. Printed page 5 and Q7 do not require that this bounded error vanish."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge classification is undetermined",
      "resolution": "The remaining ambiguity about unconditional method availability does not prevent a definite nonacceptance classification. The comparison is explicitly conditional under Q7, and the concrete extra consistency restriction already establishes loss of applicability. Source-only analytic and quantitative ambiguities remain preserved.",
      "primary_evidence": "Q7 prohibits inferring unconditional accuracy and permits exact or approximate information-only routines. Neither Q7 nor the printed paragraph following (1.11) selects the additional equality in D027."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left dependency_coverage item D008 unclear",
      "resolution": "D008 is an arbitrary method-domain predicate. Requiring membership for executed problems is appropriate for a conditional interface theorem and does not assert universal solvability. The universal hdomain premise covers every indexed face because the conclusion describes every indexed face. For a local application, Face can contain just the two required faces. Empty domains cannot satisfy this instantiated target.",
      "primary_evidence": "D008 projects Method.domain; D013 requires its proof before returning a result. The target supplies leftFace and rightFace and assumes hdomain for every face. Its location equalities and a<b imply that the selected faces are distinct."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C03 unclear",
      "resolution": "The reference and error-bound quantifier ordering is sound. The same two references support every subsequent comparison-bound instance. Supplying a routine and applicability certificates is compatible with the selected conditional workflow; it must not be advertised as proving availability from hyperbolicity alone.",
      "primary_evidence": "The fully explicit target places existential leftReference and rightReference before universal oldBound, leftComparison and rightComparison. D027 provides a reference on each permitted problem. Printed pages 5–6 give an explanatory solving workflow, not a quantified universal existence theorem."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C05 unclear",
      "resolution": "For supplied methods, the target includes all selected workflow stages and the conditional next-step estimate. Abstract incidence can represent the source's actual neighboring cells; the theorem does not itself certify a geometric mesh. This abstraction does not remove actual-grid applications. The completeness issue is resolved, while the extra method restriction remains a separate failure.",
      "primary_evidence": "D021 assigns old(leftCell face) and old(rightCell face) in order. D011 composes solve, extract and numericalFlux. D023 updates the selected cell using both numerical boundary fluxes. The explicit target includes normalized spatial averages, the exact error identity and the final conditional estimate."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item N06 unclear",
      "resolution": "Reference existence is a method premise on its domain, not a consequence of hyperbolicity. This is compatible with the conditional comparison. D029 supplies finite-slab integral solutionhood without compulsory returned fields, classical differentiability, entropy selection or uniqueness. The inherited rectangle interpretation applies to the conservation law underlying this workflow, but supplies no additional solver-existence theorem.",
      "primary_evidence": "D029 requires initial Riemann data, explicit integrability and rectangle conservation only within the positive duration. D027 existentially requires such references separately from Result. Printed Section 1.2 explicitly bases finite volume methods on (1.10), and printed page 6 permits approximate solvers."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left implication lean_implies_source unclear",
      "resolution": "Under the recorded coordinator-selected interpretation, Lean-implies-source is no in the prescribed applicability-sensitive comparison. The theorem cannot apply to permitted approximate routines with nonzero equal-state bias. Restricting such a routine's domain to unequal states does not repair coverage of equal neighboring averages.",
      "primary_evidence": "The neighboring-cell paragraph following (1.11) imposes no inequality between the two averages. D028 likewise permits equal input states, but D027 then mandates exact physical flux. Q7 permits independently bounded approximate flux errors without this mandate."
    },
    {
      "item": "Nonvacuity, normalization and dependency effects",
      "resolution": "The target is nonvacuous and its arithmetic is coherent. Positive dimension and selected inputs exclude empty-state and empty-domain applications. Positive width and duration prevent zero-denominator normalization. The supplied exact and nonexact witnesses establish useful method instances, but do not establish coverage of every routine allowed by Q7. Imported legacy solution predicates do not impose their stronger regularity requirements on this target.",
      "primary_evidence": "The native witness declarations exhibit distinct-state exact and nonexact cases with errors 0 and 1/2. D002, D022 and D024 preserve normalized integrals; the native Real.volume_Ioc declaration identifies interval volume with ENNReal.ofReal(b-a). D023 uses old-(t-s)/(b-a)•(F_right-F_left). D029, rather than the imported legacy IsIntegralConservationLawSolution predicate, defines the target's reference requirements."
    }
  ],
  "implications": {
    "lean_implies_source": {
      "verdict": "no",
      "reasoning": "Under coordinator-selected Q7 and the applicable inherited rectangle-conservation interpretation, the target preserves the local workflow and conditional error propagation only for methods satisfying its extra exact equal-state consistency premise. Q7 permits independently bounded approximation errors and does not impose that premise. Scalar advection with numerical flux u_l+δ, δ≠0, supplies a concrete excluded routine: its reference-flux error is |δ| and its conservative update satisfies the selected conditional estimate, including on equal states, but it cannot satisfy Method.consistent there. Under the audit's applicability-sensitive implication policy, this is reduced coverage, not genuine strengthening."
    },
    "source_implies_lean": {
      "verdict": "yes",
      "reasoning": "Under the recorded coordinator-selected interpretation and the applicable inherited rectangle convention, retaining all explicit and bundled Lean premises, the conditional target follows. Law supplies positive dimension and hyperbolicity; Method supplies the solver pipeline, references, error certificates and the extra equal-state equality. Normalization of the assumed physical rectangle balance yields Δx(Q_t-Q_s)=Δt(H_L-H_R). Subtracting this from the defined numerical update gives Δx(U_next-Q_t)=Δx(U_old-Q_s)+Δt[(F_L-H_L)-(F_R-H_R)]. For the fixed references, triangle inequalities give each numerical-to-physical flux bound ε+C and then the stated next-step bound. This direction does not assert that the source supplies the extra consistency premise, constructs Method, or prescribes the maximum norm."
    }
  },
  "classification": "not-faithful-weaker",
  "accepted": false,
  "remaining_uncertainties": [
    "The printed source leaves quantitative accuracy, the information representation and the discrete update formula unspecified. Q7 supplies a comparison convention; it does not turn these choices into printed assertions.",
    "The printed discontinuity discussion leaves precise trace and exceptional-time semantics implicit. The inherited receipt supports rectangle conservation in this context, without certifying arbitrary pointwise representatives or adding global evolution requirements."
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "additional-bundled-hypothesis",
      "evidence": "D027 requires exact equal-state consistency throughout the method domain. Neither printed pages 5–6, coordinator Q7, nor the inherited conservation receipt imposes this restriction. A scalar-advection flux u_l+δ with δ≠0 has a finite explicit approximation bound but violates that requirement on equal states.",
      "impact": "The target excludes otherwise eligible approximate routines. Its stronger method premise reduces applicability and prevents acceptance as faithful-equivalent or faithful-stronger."
    },
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "conditional-capability-scope",
      "evidence": "Method and hdomain are inputs; reference existence is bundled in Method.accurate. Result is arbitrary and need not contain a solution field.",
      "impact": "The theorem establishes consequences of an applicable certified routine. This conditional scope is compatible with Q7, but establishes no unconditional solver availability, uniqueness or accuracy."
    },
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "interpretation-and-provenance",
      "evidence": "The attached primary-source pages, both complete inline dossiers, dependency inventory, native declaration supplement, blind translation and both judgments were inspected without tools. The supplied hashes were not independently recomputed.",
      "impact": "The decision is qualified by the recorded interpretations and the supplied evidence boundary. Native witnesses and provenance hashes support applicability and identification, not task-specific source equivalence."
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "The decisive mismatch is the exact consistency requirement hidden in the method type, not the correctness of the conservative error calculation. Source images and declaration evidence preserve flux orientation, normalization, ordered neighboring inputs, information-only outputs and distinct numerical, reference and physical quantities. Domain and witness-order concerns resolve under the explicitly conditional interpretation without inventing a universal existence claim. Nevertheless, conditional error bounds remain meaningful for approximate routines excluded solely by Method.consistent. The prescribed classification is therefore not-faithful-weaker, with acceptance withheld and original source ambiguities retained."
}
